  "text": "```systemverilog\nmodule cdc_2phase #(\n  parameter WIDTH = 1\n)(\n  input  src_rst_ni,\n  input  src_clk_i,\n  input  [WIDTH-1:0] src_data_i,\n  input  src_valid_i,\n  output src_ready_o,\n  input  dst_rst_ni,\n  input  dst_clk_i,\n  output [WIDTH-1:0] dst_data_o,\n  output dst_valid_o,\n  input  dst_ready_i\n);\n\n  // Source domain state\n  reg src_valid_reg;\n  reg [WIDTH-1:0] src_data_reg;\n\n  // Destination domain state\n  reg dst_valid_reg;\n  reg [WIDTH-1:0] dst_data_reg;\n\n  // Handshake signals crossing domains\n  // src_to_dst_valid: source indicates it has data to send\n  // dst_to_src_ready: destination indicates it is ready to accept new data\n\n  reg src_to_dst_valid;\n  reg dst_to_src_ready;\n\n  // Synchronizers for src_to_dst_valid (2-stage)\n  reg [1:0] src_to_dst_valid_sync;\n  always @(posedge dst_clk_i or negedge dst_rst_ni) begin\n    if (!dst_rst_ni)\n      src_to_dst_valid_sync <= 2'b00;\n    else\n      src_to_dst_valid_sync <= {src_to_dst_valid_sync[0], src_to_dst_valid};\n  end\n\n  // Synchronizers for dst_to_src_ready (2-stage)\n  reg [1:0] dst_to_src_ready_sync;\n  always @(posedge src_clk_i or negedge src_rst_ni) begin\n    if (!src_rst_ni)\n      dst_to_src_ready_sync <= 2'b00;\n    else\n      dst_to_src_ready_sync <= {dst_to_src_ready_sync[0], dst_to_src_ready};\n  end\n\n  // Destination domain logic\n  // dst_valid_o is high when we have data to present\n  // We accept new data from source when dst_to_src_ready is high\n  // dst_to_src_ready is high when we are not currently holding valid data\n  //   OR when we are holding valid data and dst_ready_i is high (handshake complete)\n\n  // Let's think about this more carefully.\n  // The source can send data when src_ready_o is high.\n  // src_ready_o should be high when the destination can accept new data.\n  // The destination can accept new data when it is not currently holding a valid item,\n  //   or when it is holding a valid item and the destination is ready to consume it.\n  \n  // Actually, let's use a simpler approach:\n  // - dst_to_src_ready is high when the destination is ready to accept a new item.\n  // - The destination is ready when dst_valid_reg is low (no item held) \n  //   OR when dst_valid_reg is high and dst_ready_i is high (current item being consumed).\n  // - When dst_to_src_ready is high and src_to_dst_valid is high, a transfer occurs.\n  //   The destination captures the data and sets dst_valid_reg high.\n  //   The source clears its valid.\n\n  // Let's define:\n  // dst_can_accept = !dst_valid_reg | (dst_valid_reg & dst_ready_i)\n  // dst_to_src_ready = dst_can_accept\n\n  // When a transfer happens (src_to_dst_valid & dst_to_src_ready):\n  // - dst_data_reg <= src_data_reg (but src_data_reg is in src domain!)\n  // This is a problem. We need to transfer the data safely.\n\n  // Better approach: Use a data FIFO or a data register that is written in src domain\n  // and read in dst domain, with proper synchronization.\n\n  // Let's use a different architecture:\n  // - Source holds data in src_data_reg when src_valid_reg is high.\n  // - When src_valid_reg is high and dst_to_src_ready_sync[1] is high, a transfer is initiated.\n  // - The data is transferred via a data path that is safe for CDC.\n  //   Since we only have one outstanding item, we can use a simple approach:\n  //   The data is stable in src_data_reg while src_valid_reg is high.\n  //   The destination samples the data when it sees the valid signal transition.\n\n  // Actually, the cleanest approach for one outstanding item:\n  // - src_valid_reg is set when src_valid_i & src_ready_o.\n  // - src_ready_o = dst_to_src_ready_sync[1] (destination is ready).\n  // - When src_valid_reg is high, src_data_reg holds the data.\n  // - The valid signal src_to_dst_valid is high when src_valid_reg is high.\n  // - The destination sees src_to_dst_valid_sync[1] high.\n  // - When dst_valid_reg is low and src_to_dst_valid_sync[1] is high, the destination\n  //   captures the data and sets dst_valid_reg high.\n  // - When dst_valid_reg is high and dst_ready_i is high, the destination clears dst_valid_reg.\n  // - dst_to_src_ready is high when dst_valid_reg is low.\n  //   This way, the source can only send a new item when the destination has no item.\n\n  // But wait, this means the source can only send one item at a time, and the destination\n  // must consume it before the source can send another. This is correct for one outstanding item.\n\n  // Data transfer: The data is in src_data_reg in the src domain. The destination needs to\n  // read it. Since the data is stable while src_valid_reg is high, and the destination\n  // only samples it when it transitions from no-valid to valid, we need to ensure the data\n  // is stable long enough.\n\n  // A safer approach: Use a data register in the dst domain that is updated when a transfer\n  // occurs. But the data comes from the src domain. We can use a data synchronizer, but for\n  // multi-bit data, we need to ensure coherence.\n\n  // Since the data is stable while src_valid_reg is high, and the valid signal is synchronized,\n  // we can sample the data in the dst domain when the synchronized valid signal is high and\n  // the destination is ready to accept. The data will be stable because src_valid_reg is high\n  // and the source won't change src_data_reg until src_valid_reg is cleared.\n\n  // Let's implement this:\n\n  // Source domain\n  always @(posedge src_clk_i or negedge src_rst_ni) begin\n    if (!src_rst_ni) begin\n      src_valid_reg <= 1'b0;\n      src_data_reg  <= {WIDTH{1'b0}};\n    end else begin\n      if (src_valid_i && src_ready_o) begin\n        src_valid_reg <= 1'b1;\n        src_data_reg  <= src_data_i;\n      end else if (src_valid_reg && dst_to_src_ready_sync[1]) begin\n        // Transfer complete, clear valid\n        src_valid_reg <= 1'b0;\n      end\n    end\n  end\n\n  // src_ready_o is high when destination is ready to accept\n  assign src_ready_o = dst_to_src_ready_sync[1];\n\n  // src_to_dst_valid is high when source has data\n  assign src_to_dst_valid = src_valid_reg;\n\n  // Destination domain\n  always @(posedge dst_clk_i or negedge dst_rst_ni) begin\n    if (!dst_rst_ni) begin\n      dst_valid_reg <= 1'b0;\n      dst_data_reg  <= {WIDTH{1'b0}};\n    end else begin\n      if (!dst_valid_reg && src_to_dst_valid_sync[1]) begin\n        // Accept new data\n        dst_valid_reg <= 1'b1;\n        dst_data_reg  <= src_data_reg; // Sample data from src domain\n      end else if (dst_valid_reg && dst_ready_i) begin\n        // Handshake complete, clear valid\n        dst_valid_reg <= 1'b0;\n      end\n    end\n  end\n\n  // dst_to_src_ready is high when destination can accept new data\n  assign dst_to_src_ready = !dst_valid_reg;\n\n  // Outputs\n  assign dst_data_o  = dst_data_reg;\n  assign dst_valid_o = dst_valid_reg;\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
